 "questions": [
  "G3: the room scenes are under levels/house/rooms/ (11.1 keeps assets/ data only); the game's workflow swaps them into its greybox rooms (Body/Looks out, Shell/Dressing/Fixtures in).",
  "G11: the kit and the props are sets: one folder each (house_kit, house_props), a GLB per piece, not one GLB per folder named after it as 11.1's <id>/<id>.glb says for a single asset.",
  "Kit look and wall paints (#132): the room scenes put house_kit/kit_set.tres (the art's kit_set.gdshader, the shared set_d/set_n0/set_n1 textures and every room's wall paint) on the kit pieces' set surfaces, each mesh with its plan pose as the instance parameter plan_at; the shader is art code shipped as a file: who owns it?",
  "Imports: each file's .import here holds only ARCHITECTURE 11.2's options; the game's editor regenerates the .import files (and their uids) on its first import: commit the regenerated ones, not these.",
  "Surfaces: every walkable kit piece's instance carries metadata/surface (house.toml [export.surfaces]); the kit's GLBs carry none, so a game-side wrapper of a piece takes its surface from package.json's `surfaces`. The plot's ground (house_outdoor/outdoor.glb, package 7) is one mesh per surface (ground_grass, ground_concrete, kerb); outdoor.tscn tags each node (editable children of Ground).",
  "Lights: every fixture is a real-time OmniLight3D without shadows (20 in this package); the bake comes later (#83)."
 ]
}